Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:11:22 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): edition-aware Station Health caveat and pie
 caption

A read-only review of the 1.7.0 code against the Snapshot 2026-09-12 and
ISO 15118 data (11 agents, adversarially verified) found no blocker but:
- The Snapshot labels (2026-09-12, published) have no NO_POWER_DELIVERED
  family, so PCAP Health there reads better than on the strict labels
  (19 of 45 stations in a better band). The Stations tab and the station
  dialog now say so whenever an edition's labels lack that family.
- The fault chart caption named a data-split filter the Snapshot edition
  does not have.
- Docs: engine.json lives under each edition's product name, and the
  Snapshot edition needs the 41ded2cd checkpoints; README editions table
  updated (Snapshot 1.1.7, ISO 15118 1.3.5).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
